 "_finding": "app_main.js:3407 shows the plural to the learner on roughly half of all typing rounds for a standard noun, so a wrong pluralizeNoun result is not cosmetic --- it is drilled and graded. Italian hardens the velar in -co/-go only when the stress falls on the penultimate syllable (albergo -> alberghi) and leaves it soft otherwise (medico -> medici). Stress is not recoverable from the spelling, and the -ico/-ogo/-ago endings do not settle it either: lago, luogo, catalogo and dialogo all harden while asparago and psicologo do not. So the engine keeps the soft default and the 68 words that harden carry an explicit override, which is the pattern bosco, tacco and mollusco already used.",
